/-!
The single-adjoint core rank bound and its universal D4 level consequence.

The main theorem is `D4LevelReduction.truncatedCoreRankBound_singleAdjoint`:
for every natural `b` and every `c` with `1 ≤ c`, it proves
`TruncatedCoreRankBound 1 b c`. There are no residual cell annihilation, flag, or rank
assumptions. `levelTruncationBound_singleAdjoint_positiveCenter` gives the corresponding
universal level bound, and `singleAdjoint_interior_levelTruncationBound` states it directly
as `LevelTruncationBound m κ (κ + 2)` under `κ + 2 ≤ m`.

The coefficient flag is constructed with two simultaneous polynomial relations. Its first
relation is the existing union characteristic relation used for current truncation. Its
second relation uses the ideal generated by the adjoint characteristic and the complement
characteristic, with exponent equal to the adjoint-site difference cardinality. The same
four site transitions transport both relations on exactly the same generators and ideals.
`coreCellFlag_commonRoot_exists` proves existence for all nonnegative triples, rather than
adding an assumption to the existing flag structure. The middle raising evaluator kills
the second polynomial ideal, using the outer-root Garland relation and the one-variable
converted complete-function relation. Thus `coreCellGenerator_middle_zero_of_subset`
proves the missing zero-mode condition for every subset cell, for all triples.
For one adjoint site, `coreCell_singleAdjoint_subset_rank` applies the mixed-label bound
and obtains `15 * 6^b`.

For the other cells, the middle-raised vector has highest weight `(0, b+2, 0)` and zero
positive Cartan modes. Garland at the original vector and explicit root commutators show
that all its currents vanish at modes at least `b+1`.
`singleAdjoint_raised_rank` therefore bounds its cyclic span by `20 * 6^b` using the
doubled-site theorem. The quotient by this span has a highest vector of weight `(1, b, 1)`;
`singleAdjoint_quotient_rank` bounds that quotient by `16 * 6^b` using the local Weyl theorem.
The sum is `6^(b+2)`, yielding `coreCell_singleAdjoint_pair_rank` without further hypotheses.

The cell count and the level target are proved independently to equal
`choose (1+b+c) (b+1) * ((b+1)*15*6^b + c*6^(b+2))`.
`coreSingleAdjoint_finrank_le` sums the subset and non-subset costs along the constructed
flag. This discharges the original core rank proposition and its level consequence.

Scope: the entire one-adjoint family with positive central count is proved. Core rank bounds
with at least two adjoint sites and positive central count are outside this result; the full
D4 capstone needs those families as well.

Every main theorem has an axiom audit in its implementation module; the principal endpoints
are repeated below.
-/

